laurel 2104: console handoff. Owner bug 2026-11-01 07:20:52 (GPU on, 'direct scanout off'): when the UI is idle the panel shows kernel log text until the next frame. Cause [V, code + log]: backboardd's GL draws every other frame into surface 1 = AppleCLCD's fSurface = the boot framebuffer 0x5c000000 (RedwoodGPU 'surface 1 ... shared at 0x5c000000'; 'SWEET FB: swap 6/8/10/.../70 layer 0 surface 1'). Such a swap is not GPU-pool, so it took the copy path, which skips fSurface ('already on the panel', true only before the flip buffers) and flips to the back buffer: with GL the GPU-pool frames are scanned directly and never touch the flip buffers, so both still hold console frames from boot (sweet_console_copy_dirty while fConsShown). Every surface-1 frame showed the boot kernel log; the next GPU-pool frame covered it. The video console itself draws only into its shadow after sweet_console_retarget. Fix: (1) a single-layer swap of surface 1 is presented directly (presenter thread), the MDP scans 0x5c000000 itself; (2) at AppleCLCD start, after the MDP has latched the first console flip, the boot text in 0x5c000000 is cleared (the console text is in the shadow); (3) the copy path copies surface 1 into the back buffer like any surface, and clears a flip buffer that still holds a boot console frame before its first iOS frame; (4) at the first iOS frame one line LAUREL FB HANDOFF: self-check that the console draws into its shadow (nothing scans it; a panic shows it, sweet_cons_show); if not, console text stops being drawn (sweet_console_muted, the USB log keeps it, a panic draws). Kill switch fbhandoff=0 (no direct scan of surface 1, no clear, no self-check; the copy-path fix stays).

